{"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/Request"]},{"title":"Type Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/iatLeeway"]},{"title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/accessTokenHash(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/canonicalHtu(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/verifyProof(_:request:jtiStore:)"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"AxiamSDK"}],"title":"DpopVerifier","externalID":"s:8AxiamSDK12DpopVerifierO","roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DpopVerifier","kind":"identifier"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"DPoP proof verification — CONTRACT.md §21.7.2 (RFC 9449), contract 1.16."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DpopVerifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The resource-server half of DPoP: given the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DPoP"},{"type":"text","text":" header a caller presented, decide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether it proves possession for "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" request and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this"}]},{"type":"text","text":" access token, and return"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the key thumbprint that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AxiamRequestAuthenticator\/verifyTokenBinding(_:proofs:)"},{"type":"text","text":" then"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"matches against the token’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cnf.jkt"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Why-this-lives-in-the-SDK","type":"heading","text":"Why this lives in the SDK","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"§21.7.2 is a ten-check list, and the contract is blunt about partial implementations:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“Partial verification is worse than none, because it produces a guard that reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"success.”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" Nine of the ten look optional until someone builds an attack out of the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that was skipped, so they belong in one audited place rather than in every application","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"guarding an endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The two most often missing: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"typ"},{"text":" — without pinning it to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dpop+jwt"},{"text":", any ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"other"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" JWT","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"signed by the same key (an access token, an ID token) is replayable as a proof; and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ath"},{"text":" — without it, a proof captured on one request can be re-aimed at a different token","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"held by the same key.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-algorithm-comes-from-the-key-never-from-the-header","type":"heading","text":"The algorithm comes from the key, never from the header","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg: none"},{"text":" and RSA-public-key-as-HMAC-secret are the same bug wearing different clothes:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the token told the verifier how to check the token","type":"text"}]},{"text":". This enum dispatches on the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"embedded key’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kty"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"crv"},{"text":", so an HMAC path is never reachable no matter what the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header says.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/DpopVerifier/thumbprintS256(_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"thumbprintS256","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Any","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"]) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/dpopverifier\/thumbprints256(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/DpopVerifier\/thumbprintS256(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Compute the RFC 7638 SHA-256 thumbprint of a JWK — the ","type":"text"},{"code":"jkt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"thumbprintS256(_:)"},"doc://AxiamSDK/document